{{Quote|[&hellip;] the planet Kalee, from which the warlike Kaleesh species originated.|"[[Species From A to Z]]"|<ref name="Species From A to Z">{{GermanFanCite|115|Database}}</ref>}}
'''Kalee''' was a [[planet]] within the [[Kalee system]], a [[star system]] in [[Wild Space]] that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Kaleesh]] [[species]]. [[Grievous]], a [[Gender|male]] Kaleesh [[warlord]], was from this world.

==Description==
Kalee was a [[planet]]<ref name="Beginnings" /> located in the [[Kalee system]] of [[the galaxy]]'s [[Wild Space]], in grid square J-4 on the [[Standard Galactic Grid]].<ref name="Appendix" />

==History==
===Republic Era===
{{Quote|You're being given a rare opportunity, General Grievous&mdash;And I don't mean commanding the battle droid army. Taken from the wilds of Kalee, your body turned into a living weapon, you are the master of your own destiny.|Dooku, to Grievous|<ref name="Hyperspace Stories: Grievous">''[[Hyperspace Stories: Grievous]]''</ref>}}
The overburdened [[Galactic Republic|Old Republic]] overlooked crimes committed on the distant worlds, Kalee being one of them, and unintentionally caused injustice. The [[Yam'rii]] had brutally overran many worlds in their sector, plundering their resources and [[Slavery|enslaving]] their populations, and when the planet Kalee, [[homeworld]] of the [[Reptile|reptilian]] [[Kaleesh]] [[species]], became the center of the Yam'rii's attention, the results were horrifying: they conquered its people. The [[Kaleesh-Yam'rii war|struggle]] between the Kaleesh and the Yam'rii devolved into an ongoing war.<ref name="The Separatists">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Separatists}}</ref>

A Kaleesh named [[Grievous|Qymaen jai Sheelal]],<ref name="Build R2-D2 57">{{BuildR2Cite|57|Droid Directory}}</ref> who later became known as Grievous,<ref name="BDOWD">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Droids and Other Droids of War}}</ref> became a [[warlord]]<ref name="The Dark Side">''[[Star Wars: The Dark Side]]''</ref> and led his people<ref name="HC 8" /> in a ruthless all-war against the Yam'rii<ref name="Rise">''[[Rise of the Separatists]]''</ref> with increased vigor and determination while on the offensive. In [[time]], the Kaleesh forces successfully push the Yam'rii from their world.<ref name="The Separatists" /> Then, Grievous launched a series of devastating campaigns on the desolate planet [[Huk]],<ref name="Ships and Vehicles 55">{{ShipsandVehiclesCite|55|History of the Ship}}</ref> homeworld of the Yam'rii, and eventually, their enemies unexpectedly sought the [[Galactic Republic]] for assistance.<ref name="The Separatists" /> Then, the Republic<ref name="Rise" /> and the [[Jedi Order]] intervened in the disastrous conflict,<ref name="HC 8" /> supporting the Yam'rii<ref name="Rise" /> against the invader. The Kaleesh were condemned, embargoes and fines were imposed, and hundreds of thousands of them [[death|died]] of starvation,<ref name="The Separatists" /> causing Grievous to pursue a personal vengeance against them.<ref name="Rise" />

===Imperial Era and Age of the Resistance===
Although a [[Delphidian]] originally from the [[Delphidian Cluster]],<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> [[Sidon Ithano|Sidon]], who would eventually become the [[pirate]] Sidon Ithano,<ref name="Lost Treasure">"[[The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku]]"</ref> was raised on Kalee. At one point during the [[Imperial Era]],<ref name="LQW Tweet">{{Twitter|LandryQWalker|status/2049563168255713504|[[Landry Q. Walker]]|date=2026-04-29|quote=He didn’t just visit Kalee, he was raised there.}} {{C|In response to: "@LandryQWalker I wonder if Sidon Ithano has ever heard of General Grievous since he visited Kalee, the homeworld of the late general."}}</ref> Ithano was indoctrinated by the Kaleesh [[Elder (title)|elders]] in the [[warru'zan]], Kalee's bloodhalls, where he studied legends about [[Starweird]], a species of semi-corporeal [[Ghost (folklore)|spirits]]<ref name="Sinister Secret of the Binary Star" /> attuned to [[the Force]]<ref name="Aphra 34">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 34|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 34]]</ref> that were rumored to stalk the [[Hyperspace route|hyperspace lanes]]. Sacred rituals were then performed for him, but [[stormtrooper]]s arrived shortly afterward, and Sidon donned the [[Sidon Ithano's helmet|crimson mask]] of the trickster [[Deity|god]] [[Ithano (god)|Ithano]] for the first time.<ref name="Sinister Secret of the Binary Star" />

[[File:StronoCookieTuggs.png|thumb|left|200px|Strono Tuggs mentioned Kalee in his cookbook.]]
During a culinary tour of [[the galaxy]] that he took<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook">''[[Star Wars: The Ultimate Cookbook]]''</ref> between [[34 ABY]] and [[35 ABY]],<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook date">{{UltimateCookbookDate}}</ref> the adventurous [[chef]] [[Strono Tuggs|Strono "Cookie" Tuggs]] traveled to Kalee and traded [[Kaleesh warrior]]s some [[bantha]] cuts for minced [[karabbac]] and unearthed the ingredients necessary to cook [[Karabbac Skewer]]s. Tuggs would later include the recipe for the Skewers, as well as a retelling of his journey to Kalee, in his [[Book|cookbook]], ''[[The Ultimate Cookbook]]'',<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook" /> published in 35 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|ABY]].<ref name="Ultimate Cookbook date" />

==Inhabitants==
{{Main|Kaleesh}}
Kalee was the [[homeworld]]<ref name="Beginnings" /> of the [[Sentience|sentient]]<ref name="EpisodeIII">{{Film|III}}</ref> [[humanoid]]<ref name="KaleeshDB">{{Databank|kaleesh|Kaleesh}}</ref> reptilian<ref name="CharacterEncyclopediaUAE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> Kaleesh<ref name="Beginnings" /> species.<ref name="EpisodeIII" />

{{Planet-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Kalee was first mentioned in the current ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]] in a featurette<ref name="Liberty on Ryloth featurette">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|episode=Liberty on Ryloth}}</ref> included in [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One]], a box set available on [[Wikipedia:Blu-ray|Blu-ray]] or [[Wikipedia:DVD|DVD]] that included the entire [[The Clone Wars: Season One|first season]] of the canon animated series ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''<ref name="The Complete Season One">[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One]]</ref> that was released on [[November 3]], [[2009]].<ref name="Star Wars: The Clone Wars The Complete Season One release date">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/news20090715.html|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' The Complete Season One on DVD and Blu-Ray}}</ref>

[[Kalee/Legends|Kalee]] first originated in the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, where the planet was first mentioned in ''[[Labyrinth of Evil]]'', written by [[James Luceno]], released on [[January 25]], [[2005]],<ref name="LOE">''[[Labyrinth of Evil]]''</ref> and first appeared in "[[The Eyes of Revolution]]," a comic story written and illustrated by [[Warren Fu]], published in the [[Dark Horse Comics]] anthology ''[[Star Wars: Visionaries]]'', released on [[April 2]], [[2005]].<ref name="Eyes">{{StoryCite|story=The Eyes of Revolution|book=Star Wars: Visionaries}}</ref>

===Contradictions===
The reference booklet "[[The Separatists (reference book)|The Separatists]]" described [[Huk]] and Kalee as being located in the "Huk sector,"<ref name="The Separatists" /> but author [[Jason Fry]] has indicated this is an error.<ref name="Fry">{{EmailCite|email=File:AtlasEmail-2025-08-31.png|creator=[[Jason Fry]]|date=2025-08-31}}</ref>

